WEBVTT

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.230
Rook, you didn’t!

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:07.790
Yes, I did!

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:12.670
Orpheus bequeathed another Armlet unto me!

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.380
Orpheus did?!

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.550
I’ve made my mind. I will sacrifice
myself for Orpheus’ ideal.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:25.180
I will solve the Puzzle of
God and become a Phi-Brain!

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.560
His premonitions are absolute.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.380
No one can escape the fate
that he has foreseen!

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.760
Don’t give me that!

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:40.570
I won’t let Orpheus decide my future!

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.890
I’ll change my fate as
many times as it takes!

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:48.520
Rook, every time it comes down to it...

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:50.870
I WILL save you!

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.950
Sure enough, you’re incredible, Kaito!

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:10.210
At last, I will become
“eternal” within you!

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.870
ROOK!

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:05.030
So, You Shouldn’t Hesitate

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:15.260
Where am I?

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:22.720
I possess the intellect of the gods.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.260
I am the Phi-Brain, Orpheus.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:30.740
I will surpass the gods.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.220
How dare he show that crap to me!

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.900
Rook, I swear I won’t
let your death be in vain!

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.040
Th-then what happened to Rook...?

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:57.040
He died. That is the answer
Kaito Daimon reached.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.440
Save the bullshit!

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:02.770
There’s no freakin’ way
he’d pull a stunt like that!

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.860
You are free to doubt my words.

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:09.070
However, it does not change the
fact that Rook has fallen...

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:11.730
exactly as I foresaw.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:17.450
Cast aside petty sentiment
and aim for greater heights!

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:21.780
Defeat Kaito Daimon and become Phi-Brains.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.510
Whatcha think?

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:31.750
Of all people, I don’t want to believe
that could happen to Rook...

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.870
Freecell, how do you plan
on playin’ your hand?

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:40.020
I’m gonna finish things with Kaito!

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.130
That’s my role in all of this.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:46.070
I don’t believe it! Are you going to...?

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:52.770
This is where the Puzzle of God’s two
challengers will be determined.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:58.270
I’ll get to see you soon, my Lovushka.

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:08.530
Kaito, there is something
we would like to ask you.

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:12.300
It’s about Rook.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:15.010
That’s none of your business.

00:05:16.390 --> 00:05:18.470
Gammon... Freecell...

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.710
Guys, you should stop...
Don’t solve puzzles!

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:25.940
I’ll handle all of the puzzle solving.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:28.220
Go straight home from here!

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:41.980
You’re far too kind, Kaito.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:48.240
From the looks of it,
Orpheus was tellin’ the truth after all.

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:50.590
“Don’t solve puzzles,” huh?

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:52.380
Flush that bullshit down the toilet!

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:55.380
You’re ticking me off!

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.620
Rook can’t rest in peace
with ya actin’ like this.

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:01.600
You’re the one who needs to beat it!

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:08.380
Found it!

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:12.190
Is it the one I can just barely make out?

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:13.260
Right, that’s the one.

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:19.900
I won’t forgive Enigma or Orpheus
if they pull any dirty tricks!

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:23.200
But... the way they wanted
to go somewhere remote,

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.160
I’m afraid that’s
just what they might do.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.400
You don’t need to worry.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:28.830
Huh?

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:33.300
Haven’t they solved every puzzle so far,
no matter how hard it was?

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.790
I’m sure they’ll be fine this time, too!

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:38.340
Let’s believe in them and wait.

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:39.850
I know you’re right.

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:43.140
I know, but I have a bad feeling about this.

00:06:43.640 --> 00:06:46.920
Cut loose, Gammon!

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:50.230
Master Rook, fight!

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.480
Wh-where’d that come from?

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:53.930
I’m cheering for them! Moral support!

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:57.950
While I’m at it, hang in there, Raetsel!

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:07.210
Kaito! Freecell! Don’t lose!

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:10.000
Gammon, good luck!

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.570
Guys, good luck!

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.830
Welcome, Phi-Brain children!

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:24.460
Now we just have to wait for Raetsel.

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:26.960
That isn’t necessary!

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:30.560
You’re watching this somewhere,
aren’t you?! Orpheus!

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:32.940
There’s no need for these roundabout games!

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:34.970
Go ahead and make me your vessel already!

00:07:37.150 --> 00:07:41.040
Enigma, I know what you’re after!

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:44.030
I’ll take it all on,

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:47.230
so let’s bring this stupid farce to an end!

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:52.500
Sorry, but I can’t take
you up on that offer.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:56.980
Kaito Daimon, you lost
your best friend because

00:07:56.980 --> 00:07:59.240
you still aren’t worthy to be his vessel!

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:00.620
What?!

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:04.310
If you had truly become the ideal vessel,

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:08.500
something as simple as saving Rook’s
life would have come easy to you!

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.770
For now, you must solve this puzzle!

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.290
We can talk afterwards.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.610
Sweet! I found them!

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:22.780
What a relief! Kaito and the
others seem to be all right.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:24.660
Pino-Pino, good job!

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:26.650
Spying is such a nasty hobby.

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:30.560
I’m willing to update you on the situation
without the need for such trickery.

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:35.280
We’re about to determine which two puzzlers
will get to challenge the Puzzle of God.

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:39.670
You seem to be scampering about,
but it’s a waste of time.

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:42.840
Orpheus already knows what you have in mind.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:04.310
That’s an...

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:06.200
Armlet of Orpheus!

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.080
After all the time you’ve spent with Jin,

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:13.070
don’t you realize what that is capable of?!

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:18.070
But of course. I’m going to use this
Armlet to become a Phi-Brain.

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:21.200
I am the one who will save Jin.

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:22.880
Raetsel!

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:26.430
Well, that is all of them.

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:29.960
If you would be so kind
as to enter your lifts.

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:33.960
Kaito!

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:37.690
I’m not about to give an inch
in this upcomin’ battle!

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:40.600
I don’t care if that means
sendin’ ya to the grave!

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:42.950
Are you capable of that?

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:47.120
Do you have the determination to solve
the Puzzle of God no matter what?!

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.230
I...

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:52.290
I don’t want anyone to die.

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:54.860
It’s that plain and simple!

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:59.710
Wait, dammit! Hey!

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:01.880
Shit!

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:32.650
The puzzle you are about to solve takes
the form of a competitive battle royal.

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:38.830
Move the blocks on the field that block
your path as you race for the goal.

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:41.170
Hit the icons that appear
on the surface of the blocks

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:42.660
to make them move in that direction.

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:45.290
You cannot move the blocks immediately
after they have just moved.

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:54.350
There are two 1-man escape pods at
the goal in the center of the puzzle.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:59.440
The path to the Puzzle of God
will open to the winners.

00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:04.760
However, I expect the losers to
endure a harsh punishment.

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:13.810
Cubik, is it coming along?

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:16.250
Yeah. I’ve just about got it.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:20.380
<i>Destroy: Orpheus System.
Entering final phase.</i>

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:21.590
<i>Ouch!</i>

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:22.750
Oh, sorry!

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:24.760
Iwarin, you’re kewl!

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:27.510
Can’t we use this to save
Freecell and the others?

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:31.430
Yeah. If the Order’s ancient
manuscript was right,

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:34.710
we just need to strike the second Orpheus
tries to overtake his target...

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:40.730
<i>Warning... This mission has a
0.001% chance of success.</i>

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:42.520
<i>It’s 0.001%.</i>

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:45.640
We know that it’s dangerous, Iwashimizu!

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:48.650
Our chances certainly aren’t great!

00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:53.530
But all we can do is put our
faith in that tiny possibility!

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:57.780
<i>Roger! Roger! Roger!</i>

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.500
Right? Don’t you want to see Rae-Rae?

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:03.710
I, Ana, am very worried about Rae-Rae.

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:12.670
Well then, let puzzle time... start!

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:18.670
How dare he mess with us!
Screw his “punishment”!

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:26.440
It doesn’t matter what type of
roundabout method he uses...

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:29.430
In the end, I’ll be the
one who makes Orpheus pay!

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:37.450
There are two ways to deduce where the
others are since I can’t see them.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:40.080
One is based off where
the blocks are located.

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.460
The other is...

00:12:42.710 --> 00:12:44.040
that sound.

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:48.710
But if I take advantage of the noise,
I could confuse the others.

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:51.330
If it’s a contest of
wits, I ain’t gonna lose!

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:05.940
Jin, your long, painful journey
still isn’t over yet.

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:22.040
As long as I have my
memories of being with you,

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:24.820
I’m not afraid of anything!

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:31.510
Just wait! I’ll save you
before too much longer.

00:13:43.560 --> 00:13:47.010
Kaito and Raetsel, where
in the world are you?

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.800
The next block I need to move is...

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:55.370
I wonder why. I have a
bad feeling about this.

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:58.400
But it’s the only way that
will lead me to victory!

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:01.690
That’s it!

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:08.070
Crap!

00:14:13.130 --> 00:14:14.330
Looks like I’ve won.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.210
Not on my watch!

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:40.480
Who was that?!

00:14:40.990 --> 00:14:44.480
Raetsel. By the time I figured
it out, it was too late.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:48.210
That sucks! We’re down to only one pod.

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:53.240
For the reals?!

00:14:58.550 --> 00:14:59.800
It can’t be!

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:01.460
Thanks for sharing!

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:04.000
Hey!

00:15:08.520 --> 00:15:13.530
Gammon! Freecell! Are you okay?

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:15.890
Yeah! I’m fine!

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:19.450
Gammon! What happened?!

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:20.990
Hey, say something!

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:25.540
Shuddup! I can hear ya!

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:28.150
I screwed up...

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:34.660
Well, we’re almost there!

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:37.660
We have to push them harder and harder!

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:41.480
They must become actual Phi-Brains.

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:45.270
It’s necessary for our happy future!

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:58.530
Gammon! Freecell!

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:00.430
Leave this to me!

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:05.290
I swear I’ll find a way for all three
of us to get out of here alive!

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:09.790
A half-baked wuss like you
needs to shut the hell up!

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:11.820
What did you say?

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:17.160
Stay outta my way... I’m
gonna solve this puzzle...

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:23.960
And I, the Great Gammon Sakanoue,
will kick Orpheus’ butt!

00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:26.840
I’ve made my mind, Kaito!

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:31.020
I feel the same! It’s time
we finished things between us!

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:33.470
This isn’t the time or place for that!

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:36.740
Your whining is getting old!

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:39.470
Puzzle time isn’t over yet!

00:16:45.990 --> 00:16:47.830
Why don’t you get it?!

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:50.110
This puzzle is DIFFERENT!

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:53.490
It’s cruel, without a shred of hesitation.

00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:03.720
Even if that’s the case,
someone still has to solve this puzzle.

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:07.250
This is the last puzzle that Orpheus
included in his Trial of Puzzles.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:09.170
It’s the last trial...?

00:17:10.270 --> 00:17:13.520
Right. He’s testing us.

00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:17.010
Do we have the resolve to solve a puzzle,
even if it means sacrificing others?

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:19.360
I don’t care about his test!

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:21.020
I’m getting out of here alive!

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.740
And so are you and Gammon!

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:27.370
Sure enough, Kaito, you’re far too kind.

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:30.020
If that’s how you feel, do as you like!

00:17:32.620 --> 00:17:35.030
Let’s settle the score once and for all!

00:17:50.310 --> 00:17:52.050
I’m trapped!

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:55.190
There is no way I can turn the tables now.

00:17:55.810 --> 00:17:57.230
This is as far as I go...

00:17:58.690 --> 00:18:03.560
Kaito, thanks to you, I’ve
grown to like puzzles again.

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:07.560
Once you solve a puzzle,
you just need to start on the next one.

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:11.700
Your time started movin' long ago.

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:12.830
Freecell.

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:14.290
It wasn’t just me.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:17.320
Rook and Pinochle, Doubt and Mizerka...

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:19.340
You’ve saved so many puzzlers.

00:18:19.340 --> 00:18:24.950
I’m confident that your kindness
will become your trump card.

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:27.090
That’s won’t work...

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:29.750
Same with that.

00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:31.250
That’s out!

00:18:31.430 --> 00:18:32.520
So is that!

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:36.100
None of these hold the
answer I’m lookin’ for.

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:42.760
These don’t count as solvin’ the puzzle!

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:45.950
Where?! Where is the answer?

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:49.440
Where is the solution that
will save all three of us?!

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:00.530
Ya just barely beat me...

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:02.910
Gammon, you go on head!

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:05.540
Huh? What was that?

00:19:05.930 --> 00:19:08.130
You should go first since you’re injured!

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:10.290
I’ll catch up later with Freecell.

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:14.800
“Catch up,” my ass!
You’re already at a loss.

00:19:15.350 --> 00:19:18.270
Shuddup! Shut your trap and do what I--

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:30.890
Gammon!

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:33.450
Gammon, are you okay?!

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:36.000
Yeah, amazingly enough...

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:38.620
Hang tight! I’ll get you out right now!

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:42.590
Don’t worry ’bout me.

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:46.590
You’ll never find the type of
answer you’re lookin’ for here.

00:19:47.090 --> 00:19:49.260
Only one of us gets to survive.

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:51.760
That’s the way this puzzle works.

00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:52.960
Don’t be stupid!

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:56.060
You have no right to give up!

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:59.060
I’m not gonna let anyone die!

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:02.970
You don’t know when to give up...

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:06.350
It’s about time you manned up!

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:09.660
Aren’t you gonna solve all the puzzles?!

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:12.530
Solve the puzzle, Kaito.

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:18.280
You’re the only one who can
rewrite that future of ruin...

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:20.040
Gammon...

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:22.880
Kaito!

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:27.670
Don’t you remember how you
told me to solve puzzles?

00:20:28.630 --> 00:20:30.380
So you shouldn’t hesitate!

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:33.290
Solve it! Solve the Puzzle of God!

00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:37.060
Guys...

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:43.050
That was excellent.

00:20:43.730 --> 00:20:46.150
Let’s bring this to a close with a bang.

00:21:01.290 --> 00:21:02.440
Damn it...

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:05.570
Gammon! Freecell!

00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:09.010
Go, Kaito!

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:13.470
Get going, Kaito!

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:18.960
Don’t hesitate!

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:20.980
Go!

00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:34.700
Gammon...

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:36.780
Kaito... Freecell...

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:39.480
Wait!

00:21:45.420 --> 00:21:46.840
Th-thank you.

00:21:47.090 --> 00:21:49.000
Mr. Pinochle, what’s this?

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:51.870
Oh, it’s a puzzle that Freecell made.

00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:55.580
It’s one of his favorites, so
I thought I’d take it to him.

00:21:56.260 --> 00:21:59.340
Is that right? It’s a
nice puzzle, isn’t it?

00:22:10.570 --> 00:22:13.530
The future is converging.

00:22:14.070 --> 00:22:17.780
Despite how you struggle,
it can no longer be altered.

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:22.110
All of the pieces have come together.

00:22:22.660 --> 00:22:25.420
At long last, the time has come!

00:24:02.010 --> 00:24:05.350
Down with Orpheus! We need
to set up a plan, huh?

00:24:05.350 --> 00:24:06.770
You can leave that to me, Ana!

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:08.230
I’ll go “Boo!”

00:24:08.230 --> 00:24:11.690
And when they bring out the fluffy-fluffy,
I should go “kaboom,” right?

00:24:11.690 --> 00:24:12.840
What’s that supposed to mean?

00:24:12.840 --> 00:24:15.050
He has a 100% chance of success.

00:24:15.050 --> 00:24:16.320
You understood that?!

00:24:16.320 --> 00:24:18.240
Next time, “The Two of Us!”

00:24:16.370 --> 00:24:27.960
The Two of Us!

00:24:18.450 --> 00:24:19.860
Lend me a hand, Robot!

00:24:19.860 --> 00:24:21.140
All of the girls are holding a party!

00:24:21.140 --> 00:24:23.030
Girl’s party! Girl’s party!

00:24:23.030 --> 00:24:24.660
Why are you doing that?!

00:24:24.660 --> 00:24:27.000
Girl’s party!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin
Art: Akeru Otsuki
